            "url": "https://fortune.com/2017/08/04/trade-deficit-export/",
            "title": "U.S. Exports Increased in June but So Did the U.S.-China Trade ...",
            "snippets": [
              "# U.S. Exports Increased in June but So Did the U.S.-China Trade Deficit\nThe Commerce Department said on Friday the trade gap decreased 5.9% to $43.6 billion, the lowest level since October 2016. May’s trade deficit was revised slightly down to $46.4 billion from the previously reported $46.5 billion.\n\nEconomists polled by Reuters had forecast the trade shortfall narrowing to $45.0 billion in June",
              "When adjusted for inflation, the trade deficit fell to $61.0 billion from $62.8 billion in May. Real goods exports surged to an all-time high of $126.9 billion in June, buoyed by record high petroleum exports.\n\nThe government reported last Friday that trade contributed almost two-tenths of a percentage point to the economy’s 2.6% annualized growth pace in the second quarter",
              "In June, exports of goods and services increased 1.2% to $194.4 billion, the highest level since December 2014. There were increases in exports of capital goods, food and motor vehicles. Exports to China fell 4.7%",
              "Imports of goods and services slipped 0.2% to $238.0 billion in June. There were decreases in imports of industrial supplies and materials. Imports of cell phones and other household goods fell $0.9 billion, accounting for the bulk of the $0.7 billion decrease in consumer goods imports.\n\nImports of goods from China increased 1.2%. The politically sensitive U.S.-China trade deficit increased 3.1% to $32.6 billion in June",
              "{\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"Fortune\"},\"articleSection\":\"Finance\",\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Lisa Fu\"}],\"dateModified\":\"2017-08-04T15:45:31-00:00\",\"datePublished\":\"2017-08-04T14:51:20-00:00\",\"description\":\"The US increased exports of capital goods, food and automobiles but imports from China also increased 1.2%.\",\"headline\":\"U.S. Exports Increased in June but So Did the U.S.-China Trade Deficit\",\"identifier\":2112683,\"keywords\":[\"China\",\"International\",\"Tariffs\"],\"isAccessibleForFree\":false,\"hasPart\":{\"isAccessibleForFree\":\"False\"},\"stnMeta\":{\"bmb\":\"bmb\",\"campaign\":\"campaign\",\"ch\":\"finance\",\"cid\":\"2112683\",\"franchise\":\"franchise\",\"tags\":[\"china\",\"international\",\"tariffs\"]}}"
            ]
