            "url": "https://www.usnews.com/news/economy/articles/2017-07-06/us-trade-deficit-with-china-widens-as-north-korea-showdown-looms",
            "title": "U.S. Trade Deficit With China Widens as North Korea Showdown Looms",
            "snippets": [
              "# U.S. Trade Deficit With China Widens as North Korea Showdown Looms\nBillions of dollars in trade hang in the balance as the U.S. reportedly weighs retaliation against China for doing business with North Korea.",
              "America's trade deficit contracted slightly in May but was still considerably larger through the first five months of 2017 than it was a year prior.\n\nBut as trade officials under President Donald Trump gear up for a possible showdown with China over Chinese-North Korean commerce, the latest export and import data show a significant share of U.S. trade potentially hangs in the balance",
              "### ADP: U.S. Job Growth Slows to 158K\nExports through the first five months of the year clocked in at nearly $958 billion, up more than $54 billion from the same period a year ago. Imports, meanwhile, hit nearly $1.2 trillion, an increase of more than $81 billion",
              "\"Of note, the trade deficit with key trading partners, including Canada, Mexico and China, are all wider year-to-date compared to the same period in 2016 – a development which will likely heighten the protectionist rhetoric coming from Washington,\" a team of researchers at Oxford Economics wrote in a research note Thursday",
              "At issue for Trump is a trade report published this week that suggests Chinese trade with North Korea was up 15 percent during the first five months of the year – though that increase was driven largely by North Korea buying Chinese products. Chinese purchases of North Korean exports appeared to have cooled",
              "### With Job Creation Slowing, Who's Hiring?\nFor years, China has been the single largest importer of products into the U.S. – and one of its most lopsided trading partners. America's trade deficit with China in goods and services through the first quarter of the year rose to nearly $82 billion – a larger value than America's deficits with Germany, Japan, Mexico, India, Italy and Taiwan over that period combined",
              "In the first three months of 2017 alone, China imported more than $127 billion of goods and services into the U.S",
              "### Report: Bannon Pushing for Tax Hike on Wealthy\nSeveral members of Trump's Cabinet reportedly expressed opposition to the plan, but it is as of yet unclear whether the president will follow through. The ultimate concern is that actions against China would lead to higher prices for consumers and reduced international selling options for American producers.\n\nThose concerns are mitigated for some, though, by the sheer size of America's trade deficit with China and the fact that commerce pressures between the two countries have been bubbling for years",
              "\"I think over time, there inevitably is going to be significant conflict [between the U.S. and China]. If you look at U.S. trade relations around the world, China does stand out. We have by far our biggest trade deficit with China,\" Harris said. \"This is an area where actually there's common agreement among economists and policymakers in the U.S"
            ]
